# ML Core layer for macOS Intel (Darwin x86_64)
# Target-owned lockfile for deterministic pip-compile resolution.
#
# This file is macOS-specific because pip-compile cannot resolve
# conditional dependencies across platforms in a single graph.
#
# This target is frozen pending an authoritative Darwin x86_64 lane decision.
#
# PLATFORM TARGET: darwin-x86_64-cpu (macOS Intel)
#
# IMPORTANT:
# This lock input remains intentionally conservative because PyTorch 2.4+
# wheels are not available for macOS Intel in the supported environment.
# In practice that means:
# - keep torch at 2.2.x for macOS Intel wheel availability
# - keep numpy<2 to avoid ABI breaks against torch 2.2.x extensions
# - keep transformers<5 so the torch backend remains usable with torch 2.2.x
#
# SECURITY NOTE (CVE-2025-32434):
#   torch < 2.6.0 has a critical RCE vulnerability via torch.load()
#   This frozen lane is not a supported remediation target. weights_only=True
#   remains mandatory defense in depth, but it is not considered a complete
#   fix for this historical torch baseline.
#
# See: requirements/README.md for layering rationale.

# --- PyTorch (macOS, deterministic) ---
# CAS DETERMINISM: Pinned versions for reproducible environment fingerprints
# SECURITY: frozen unsupported lane; do not treat runtime hardening as a fix
torch==2.2.2  # CAS determinism: cross-platform reproducibility
torchvision==0.17.2  # CAS determinism: matches torch 2.2.2

# NumPy guardrail for the conservative Darwin torch 2.2.x baseline.
numpy<2

# Diffusion / HuggingFace ecosystem
diffusers>=0.36.0,<1
transformers>=4.57.0,<5
huggingface-hub>=0.19.0,<2
accelerate>=0.20.0,<2

